# Git remotes — GitHub first, GitLab when host is pnmac

`LoanOps-Agent` origin is GitHub (`github.com/mohit-bohra-dev/LoanOps-Agent`).

1. **This repo (PRs, issues, pipeline on origin):** `gh`. Do not default to `glab` or GitLab MCP.
2. **`gitlab.pnmac.com` (EAKG clones, enterprise app repos):** `glab` first. GitLab MCP only if `glab` missing, auth fail, or no `glab` equivalent.
3. Read host from `git remote get-url origin` (or the remote you are operating on). `github.com` → `gh`. `gitlab.pnmac.com` → `glab`.

Do not apply `feature/{env}/{name}` branching from other Promp git packages. This repo uses conventional commits (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`) on working branches. Jira keys in commits only when the user gives a ticket.

## Command map (this repo)

| Intent | Tool |
|---|---|
| Create PR | `gh pr create` |
| View PR | `gh pr view` |
| PR comment | `gh pr comment` |
| Checks | `gh pr checks` |

## Command map (`gitlab.pnmac.com`)

| Intent | `glab` |
|---|---|
| Verify project / default branch | `glab repo view --output json` |
| Create MR | `glab mr create --title "…" --description "…" --target-branch {target} [--draft]` |
| View MR | `glab mr view {iid}` / `glab mr view {iid} --comments` |
| MR note | `glab mr note {iid} --message "…"` |
| Pipeline / job | `glab ci status` / `glab ci list` / `glab ci trace {job}` |

Local `git` still owns branch / commit / push.
